# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# Windows reserved device name — created accidentally when a command meant
# for cmd.exe's null-device redirect (e.g. `> nul`, `2>nul`) runs under
# Git Bash/MSYS instead, which doesn't special-case "nul" and just creates
# a literal file. Git can't index it (short read on the reserved name), so
# it's ignored here as a safety net rather than relied on to never recur.
/nul

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# dev-server output redirected to a file during manual verification
# (npm run dev > dev-out.log 2> dev-err.log) — scratch, never committed
dev-out.log
dev-err.log

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# local review screenshots (visual QA during a stage, never committed)
/.review/

# local agent/tooling config — machine-specific, not part of the app
/.agents/
/.claude/
/skills-lock.json

# reference/inspiration images (third-party template screenshots) — kept
# locally for design reference only, never committed
docs/**/*.webp
docs/**/*.jpg
docs/**/*.jpeg
docs/**/*.png

# raw video source/placeholders — GitHub's 100MB file limit rejects these
# outright (public/video-placeholder.mov was 755MB and blocked a push);
# real, web-sized video assets belong in Sanity or a CDN, not git. If a
# genuinely small, final video needs to ship from /public, add an explicit
# exception for that one file rather than removing this rule.
public/**/*.mov
public/**/*.mp4
public/**/*.webm

# source scans containing PII (codice fiscale, home address) awaiting
# redaction/review — never committed, see contents/redacted/ for the
# redacted exports this generates
/contents/

# parallax diagnostic output
parallax-*.png

# Partner research: named firms with commercial judgements on them ("do not
# use", "competitor for our own traffic"). The repository is PUBLIC, and docs/
# is tracked, so committing this would publish those judgements — findable by
# the very firms it names. The file stays on disk and out of git.
docs/partners-*.md

# DataForSEO raw responses — intermediate measurement output, regenerated by
# the scripts in scripts/dataforseo/ for a few cents. The dossiers written from
# it live in docs/; the raw JSON is large, dated and of no use to a reader.
/.dfs/

# SEO dossiers: they name competitors, say which of their positions we intend
# to take, and quote our own standing. Same reason docs/partners-*.md stays
# out — the repository is PUBLIC and docs/ is tracked, so committing these
# publishes a competitive plan to the domains it names. Regenerating one costs
# under a dollar from the scripts in scripts/dataforseo/.
docs/seo-*.md

# Outreach drafts: they name a target publication or firm and say what we
# want from it. Same reason docs/partners-*.md and docs/seo-*.md stay out —
# the repository is PUBLIC, and the people named would be the ones to find it.
docs/outreach-*.md
